===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Someone or something that [[catches]].
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The player that squats behind [[home plate]] and receives the pitches from the [[pitcher]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=13-02-1989|author=Roger Angell|journal=Season Ticket: A Baseball Companion|page=22|publisher=Ballantine Books
|passage=Finding Dempsey in my mind's eye in January was not quite startling, ''...''but some other '''catchers''' turned up in my hot-stove reveries as well. Bob Boone, for instance.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=John E. Peterson|title=The Kansas City Athletics: A Baseball History: 1954–1967|location=Jefferson, NC|publisher=w:McFarland & Company|isbn=9780786416103|page={{gbooks|U1yPcpoEi_8C|210|pitchometer}}|passage=A “pitchometer” was installed on the scoreboard to time the pitchers. According the baseball rules a pitcher had to throw a pitch within 20 seconds after he received the ball from the '''catcher''' when there was nobody on base.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2021|work=Course Hero|title=The plate umpire may suspend play because of darkness|author=University of the District of Columbia|volume=|number=|passage=At the plate the '''catcher''' is responsible for catching pitches, keeping mispitched balls in front of the plate, calling pitches that are normally done through hand signals, picking off runners, and they are considered the leaders of the field.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|US|colloquial}} The [[bottom]] partner in a [[homosexual]] [[relationship]] or [[sexual]] [[encounter]] between two men.
#: {{syn|en|bottom}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[wrestler]].

